# API Data Fetching & Caching

## Architecture Overview
- **API Routes**: Next.js API routes in `app/api/`
- **Service Layer**: [services/apiService.ts](mdc:services/apiService.ts) for API calls
- **Cache Layer**: [hooks/useApiCache.ts](mdc:hooks/useApiCache.ts) with React Query
- **Preloading**: [services/dataPreloader.ts](mdc:services/dataPreloader.ts) for background loading

## API Endpoints
- `/api/layouts` - Get all kitchen layouts
- `/api/materials` - Get all countertop materials
- `/api/edge-styles` - Get all edge styles
- `/api/layout-fields/[layoutId]` - Get measurement fields for layout
- `/api/auto-calculation-rules/[layoutId]` - Get calculation rules
- `/api/layout-field-groups/[layoutId]` - Get field groups

## React Query Hooks
```typescript
// Basic usage
const { data: layouts, isLoading, error } = useLayouts();
const { data: fields } = useLayoutFields(layoutId);
const { data: materials } = useMaterials();
const { data: edgeStyles } = useEdgeStyles();
```

## Preloaded Data Priority
All hooks automatically use preloaded data when available:
```typescript
// Hook implementation
queryFn: async () => {
  const preloadedData = dataPreloader.getPreloadedData();
  if (preloadedData) {
    return preloadedData.layouts; // Use preloaded data
  }
  return apiService.getLayouts(); // Fallback to API
}
```

## Cache Configuration
- **Stale Time**: 1-2 hours for static data
- **GC Time**: 24 hours for garbage collection
- **Enabled**: Conditional based on required parameters

## Error Handling
```typescript
// Service layer error handling
try {
  const response = await fetch('/api/layouts');
  if (!response.ok) {
    throw new Error('Failed to fetch layouts');
  }
  return await response.json();
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Error fetching layouts:', error);
  return []; // Return empty array as fallback
}
```

## Background Preloading
- Starts immediately when homepage loads
- Fetches all data in parallel
- Stores in Zustand store via callback
- Completely invisible to users

## Performance Patterns
- **Parallel Fetching**: Multiple API calls in parallel
- **Conditional Fetching**: Only fetch when needed
- **Caching**: React Query handles cache invalidation
- **Fallback**: Graceful degradation if preloading fails

## Type Safety
All API responses are typed with TypeScript interfaces:
```typescript
interface Layout {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  layout_image: string;
  // ... other properties
}
```
